Z||000000||kevin||03-02-2001||01:41 AM||||Has anybody considered replacing the 2.5 Duke with the turbo engine from the same year Pontiac Sunfire? I do not know if this engine bolts up to the Izusu 5-speed or the Getrag? Hey guys, any ideas?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tweek||03-02-2001||02:10 AM||||I was given an article by another forum member on this subject. Apparently 11 cars were equipped with the 2.0 turbo (found on 89-90 Sunbird GT) by Red Shift Ltd. right from the factory. They came with the 5 speed Getrag. Now, (for this example I'll use my 84) If the 2.0 turbo bolts up to the Getrag, and the 2.5 also bolts to the Getrag, then the 2.0 turbo in theory should bolth right up to my 125c. Of course, there is probably something preventing this from being so easy...  but hey going from 90 hp to 165 would be a definate imporovement...  anyone else's thoughts???||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric_PA||03-02-2001||09:44 AM||||The starter is mounted on the opposite side on the 2.0 OHC Sunbird engine. I know this cause I was going to transplant the transmission from the Sunbird to my Fiero when it died on me. My guess would be you have to transplant the transmission along wiht the engine. <BR>Eric<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||03-02-2001||11:22 AM||||If you are going to that much trouble, stick the biggest dang engine in there you can afford. I consider the 2.0L T-SB engine to be a marginal improvement although it would be a clean installation. Zip for torque.<P>The problem is that J-cars are torque axis mounted so you'd have to fabricate a lower crank side mount. I wonder if an N car mount would work (Turbo Grand Am). Are N cars torque axis?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula 18||03-02-2001||09:13 PM||||I think that that would be a cool swap too. I was thinking it would be a good way to replace a dead (iron) duck.  I have a FOCCA article coomparing a SD4, a v6 turbo to this 2.0 Turbo and It say it will run a 14.60 quarter mile with the matching getrag.<P>Watch out! I have heard that the early 2.0 block had diffrent belling housing depending on if it's an stick or an auto. I seems like I remeber the auto having on less bolt. <P><BR>" The problem is that J-cars are torque axis mounted so you'd have to fabricate a lower crank side mount. I wonder if an N car mount would work (Turbo Grand Am). Are N cars torque axis?" <P>Terry You want to elaborate on this?? <P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula 18||03-02-2001||09:17 PM||||One more note. <P>2.0L turbo<BR>165 HP @ 5600rpm<BR>175 ft/lbs. @ 400 rpm<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tweek||03-02-2001||11:01 PM||||I believe thats 175 ft/lbs @ 4000 rpm.... :-)||||reg||1
